{"tool_name":"open-sim_moco","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:open-sim_moco"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"Open-Sim_Moco","home":"https://simtk.org/projects/opensim-moco","summary":"Musculoskeletal optimal control.\n\nOpenSim Moco solves optimal control problems with musculoskeletal models defined in OpenSim, using direct collocation.\n\nOpenSim Moco is a software toolkit to solve optimal control problems with musculoskeletal models defined in OpenSim, including those with kinematic constraints. Using the direct collocation method, Moco can solve a wide range of problems, including motion tracking, motion prediction, and parameter optimization. The design of Moco focuses on ease-of-use, customizability, and extensibility. Just like OpenSim itself, Moco has interfaces in XML/command-line, Matlab, Python, Java, and C++.","addition_date":"2020-01-14T09:07:51Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:30:48.665342Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:Open-Sim_Moco","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"Open-Sim Moco","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/839381","type":["Preprint"]},{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1008493","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Zoology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3500"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:open-sim_moco/cmd/simtk.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/839381","pmcid":null,"pmid":null,"ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":null,"year":null}]},{"entries":[{"cit_count":92,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":2020},{"count":7,"year":2021},{"count":12,"year":2022},